    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0554" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4419: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan (Forbes) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-26T17:00:00+09:00">February 26, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 26—5:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. I have conferred with the British and Italian Ambassadors and communicated
                    with the French Ambassador in regard to your telegram No. 62;<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d486-f1"/> and they, under their instructions, do not feel either a
                    joint visit or identic note feasible. They are calling individually on the
                    Minister. I have accordingly left a memorandum with the Foreign Minister in
                    writing in accordance with your instructions, as near as we could make it word
                    for word a copy of which will be sent by mail. The Foreign Minister received me
                    and stated that the representations of the United States would receive his most
                    careful consideration and that <pb facs="0555" n="451" xml:id="pg451"/> he would
                    refer the matter immediately to the proper department and let us hear from him
                    later.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Forbes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
